# Error handling

- Map API failures to calm, actionable copy (retry / check connection / contact support).
- Never dump raw payloads or stack traces in the UI.
- Distinguish **empty · loading · forbidden (no grant) · error**.
- Missing DataGrant ≠ error — dedicated empty copy (“Member has not shared X”).
- Log details server-side only when logging exists.

## Server Actions

- Actions return a typed result (`{ ok: true } | { ok: false; code; message }`) — they do not throw into JSX.
- Branch on the API `error.code`; map to copy in `lib/modules/<module>/<module>-errors.ts`. Never invent codes.
- Every mutation surfaces a **visible** failure state. No silent `.catch(() => {})`.
- Zod validation failures map back to the offending field where the form allows it — not one generic toast for a 5-field form.
